{"title":"Career Roadmap — QA Tester","role":"QA Tester","summary":"A QA Tester (Quality Assurance Tester) validates software applications to identify defects, verify requirements, evaluate usability, and ensure that software works reliably before and after release.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Computer Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A QA Tester (Quality Assurance Tester) validates software applications to identify defects, verify requirements, evaluate usability, and ensure that software works reliably before and after release."},{"type":"p","text":"Modern QA is much broader than manually clicking through an application. A future-ready QA professional should understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Software Testing","Programming","Automation","APIs","SQL","CI/CD","Cloud","Quality Engineering"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Manual Tester","QA Engineer","Automation Engineer","Senior QA Engineer","SDET/QA Lead","Quality Engineering Manager"],"label":"The career can progress from"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Development Focus","Typical Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Testing fundamentals, SQL, programming, manual testing"},{"text":"QA Intern / Test Intern"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Functional testing, API testing, automation"},{"text":"QA Tester / QA Engineer"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Test automation, CI/CD, performance and security testing"},{"text":"Automation QA Engineer / SDET"}],[{"text":"2037–2041"},{"text":"Test architecture, quality strategy and technical leadership"},{"text":"Senior QA Engineer / QA Lead"}],[{"text":"2041–2046"},{"text":"Engineering quality strategy and team leadership"},{"text":"QA Manager / Quality Engineering Manager"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Programming & CS Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Programming fundamentals"},{"text":"OOP"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Basic algorithms"},{"text":"DBMS"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Operating systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one primary programming language:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Java"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"JavaScript/TypeScript"},{"text":"Java or Python are particularly useful for test automation."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git"},{"text":"GitHub"},{"text":"Command line basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Testing Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Software Development Life Cycle"},{"text":"Software Testing Life Cycle"},{"text":"Test planning"},{"text":"Test cases"},{"text":"Test scenarios"},{"text":"Test data"},{"text":"Defect reporting"},{"text":"Regression testing"},{"text":"Smoke testing"},{"text":"Sanity testing"},{"text":"Functional testing"},{"text":"Integration testing"},{"text":"System testing"},{"text":"Acceptance testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Verification vs Validation"},{"type":"p","text":"and"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Assurance vs Quality Control vs Testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Automation & Quality Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus heavily on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automation testing"},{"text":"API testing"},{"text":"Database testing"},{"text":"Performance testing"},{"text":"CI/CD"},{"text":"Test frameworks"},{"text":"Selenium/Playwright"},{"text":"Postman"},{"text":"JUnit/PyTest"},{"text":"Docker fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how testing fits into a modern development pipeline:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Code","Build","Unit Tests","Integration Tests","API Tests","UI Tests","Security / Performance Checks","Deployment","Production Monitoring"]}]},{"heading":"Manual Testing Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Even automation-focused QA engineers need strong testing fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Functional Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Features"},{"text":"Business rules"},{"text":"User workflows"},{"text":"Input validation"},{"text":"Error handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Regression Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Verify that new changes haven't broken existing functionality."},{"type":"h","text":"Smoke Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Quickly determine whether a build is stable enough for deeper testing."},{"type":"h","text":"Exploratory Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Use structured investigation rather than only following predefined test cases."},{"type":"h","text":"Usability Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Evaluate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"User experience"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Error messages"},{"text":"Interaction consistency"}]}]},{"heading":"Test Case Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn professional techniques such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Equivalence Partitioning"},{"type":"p","text":"Divide inputs into meaningful groups and test representative values."},{"type":"h","text":"Boundary Value Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Test values around boundaries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Minimum"},{"text":"Minimum + 1"},{"text":"Valid Middle"},{"text":"Maximum - 1"},{"text":"Maximum"},{"text":"Maximum + 1"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Decision Tables"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful when multiple conditions determine the outcome."},{"type":"h","text":"State Transition Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for systems where behaviour changes based on state."},{"type":"h","text":"Pairwise Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for efficiently testing combinations of multiple parameters."}]},{"heading":"Defect Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A QA Tester must be able to communicate defects clearly."},{"type":"p","text":"A good defect report should contain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Title"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Preconditions"},{"text":"Steps to reproduce"},{"text":"Expected result"},{"text":"Actual result"},{"text":"Severity"},{"text":"Priority"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Build/version"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirement","Test Scenario","Test Case","Execution","Defect Found","Bug Report","Developer Fix","Retesting","Regression Testing","Closure"]}]},{"heading":"Automation Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Automation is one of the most important areas for career growth."},{"type":"h","text":"Selenium"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WebDriver"},{"text":"Locators"},{"text":"XPath"},{"text":"CSS selectors"},{"text":"Waits"},{"text":"Page Object Model"},{"text":"Screenshots"},{"text":"Test suites"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Playwright"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern web testing skills can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Browser automation"},{"text":"Cross-browser testing"},{"text":"Parallel execution"},{"text":"Network interception"},{"text":"API testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cypress"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand its use for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frontend testing"},{"text":"End-to-end testing"},{"text":"Component testing"},{"text":"A student does not need to master all three. One framework deeply + another at awareness level is sufficient initially."}]}]},{"heading":"Programming for QA","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"Target","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"h","text":"Java"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful stack:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Java","OOP","Collections","JUnit","Selenium / Playwright","Maven / Gradle"]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful stack:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Python","OOP","pytest","Selenium / Playwright","Requests","Automation Framework"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn programming well enough to build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reusable test utilities"},{"text":"Test frameworks"},{"text":"Data generators"},{"text":"API automation"},{"text":"Reporting tools"}]}]},{"heading":"API Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"API testing is essential for modern QA."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HTTP"},{"text":"REST"},{"text":"JSON"},{"text":"XML basics"},{"text":"GET"},{"text":"POST"},{"text":"PUT"},{"text":"PATCH"},{"text":"DELETE"},{"text":"Status codes"},{"text":"Headers"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Tokens"},{"text":"Request/response validation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Postman"},{"text":"Newman"},{"text":"REST Assured"},{"text":"Python Requests"},{"text":"Playwright API testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"}]},{"heading":"Database Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"SQL is extremely valuable for QA."},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"HAVING"},{"text":"ORDER BY"},{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window Functions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use SQL to verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Records created correctly"},{"text":"Data updates"},{"text":"Data deletion"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Referential integrity"},{"text":"Backend calculations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Action","Frontend","API","Database","Stored Data"]},{"type":"p","text":"QA should be able to verify each layer."}]},{"heading":"Performance Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Load testing"},{"text":"Stress testing"},{"text":"Spike testing"},{"text":"Endurance testing"},{"text":"Scalability testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Response time"},{"text":"Throughput"},{"text":"Concurrent users"},{"text":"Error rate"},{"text":"Resource utilization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools to explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JMeter"},{"text":"k6"},{"text":"Gatling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"Intermediate"}]},{"heading":"Security Testing Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"QA professionals should understand basic application security."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Authentication testing"},{"text":"Authorization testing"},{"text":"Session management"},{"text":"Input validation"},{"text":"Password security"},{"text":"Access control"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with common web risks such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL injection"},{"text":"Cross-site scripting"},{"text":"Broken access control"},{"text":"Insecure authentication"},{"text":"For dedicated security testing, deeper cybersecurity specialization is required."}]}]},{"heading":"CI/CD & DevOps","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern QA should integrate testing into deployment pipelines."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git"},{"text":"GitHub/GitLab"},{"text":"GitHub Actions"},{"text":"Jenkins fundamentals"},{"text":"Docker"},{"text":"CI/CD concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Developer Push","CI Pipeline","Build","Unit Tests","API Tests","UI Automation","Test Report","Deployment"]}]},{"heading":"Five Recommended UG Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — E-Commerce Testing Framework"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a sample e-commerce application and create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Test plan"},{"text":"Test scenarios"},{"text":"Test cases"},{"text":"Defect reports"},{"text":"Regression suite"},{"text":"Automated UI tests"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"h","text":"Java/Python + Selenium/Playwright"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — API Automation Framework"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an automation suite for a REST API."},{"type":"p","text":"Test:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"CRUD operations"},{"text":"Validation"},{"text":"Error responses"},{"text":"Status codes"},{"text":"Response schemas"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Python","pytest","Requests"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"h","text":"Java + REST Assured"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Database Testing Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a small application with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frontend"},{"text":"API"},{"text":"Database"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Write tests verifying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data creation"},{"text":"Updates"},{"text":"Deletion"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Transaction behaviour"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"h","text":"SQL + Python/Java"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — CI/CD Automated Testing Pipeline"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a GitHub repository where every code push automatically:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Builds Application","Runs Unit Tests","Runs API Tests","Runs UI Tests","Generates Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GitHub Actions"},{"text":"Docker"},{"text":"Playwright/Selenium"},{"text":"pytest/JUnit"},{"text":"This is an excellent portfolio project."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Performance Testing Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Use JMeter or k6 to test an application under different loads."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Response time"},{"text":"Throughput"},{"text":"Error rate"},{"text":"Concurrent users"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a dashboard using:"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel / Power BI / Python"}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"QA Internships"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QA Tester Intern"},{"text":"Software Testing Intern"},{